## 🚀 Core Module Specifications

### 🤖 1. AI Assistant Portal & Ingestion Engine
Allows immediate parsing and generation of global intelligence records. Contains explicit data structures to log structured data feeds right into the persistent engine, supporting restricted distribution visibility rules (Premium vs. Draft).

### 🌍 2. Customs Tariff Engine (AHTN Compliance)
An automated customs nomenclature engine tracking trade operations. It ingests standard 6-digit commodity markers and formats them directly into **8-Digit precision strings (`081340.00`)**, ensuring compliance bounds match ASEAN Zone structural rules.

### 📈 3. Greencore Coordinate Scale (Enterprise Tier)
An enterprise-grade operating module layer designed to oversee green trade network loops at scale. It embeds specialized components for:
* Enterprise Procurement Pipelines
* Advanced AI-Assisted Supplier Comparison Matrices
* Cargo Telemetry Monitoring Requests
* End-to-End International Logistics Coordination

---

## 🛠️ Local Deployment & Startup Flow

### 📋 Prerequisites
Ensure your host machine has Node.js (LTS), PM2, and Python 3 installed.

### 1. Launch the Cluster Environments on your Ubuntu Server
Initialize your background application processes under persistent daemon controls:
```bash
# Step into the repository directory root
cd /home/tx/tradexpress-app

# Install explicit database configuration drivers
npm install mysql2 sqlite3 express cors

# Fire up and register the dual-engine process array
pm2 start server.js --name "kenwell-tx-core-engine"
pm2 start Kenwell.py --name "kenwell-tx-python-proxy" --interpreter python3

# Lock the configuration into PM2 daemon memory records
pm2 save
```

### 2. Access the Visual Workspaces
* **OS Telemetry Panel (Cockpit)**: Navigate your web browser to `https://192.168.100.11:9090` to visually inspect CPU, Memory, and System Services streams.
* **Control Dashboard**: Right-click `src/components/tradexpress-workspace.html` on your desktop machine and open it natively inside Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge. Set your selector node to **Port 8000** to execute live data pings.

---

## 🛡️ Enterprise Development Sign-Off Rules
* **Code Signing Privacy**: Always sign local Git contributions using your anonymous fallback obfuscation email string (`id+username@users.noreply.github.com`) to protect server network metadata profiles.
* **Database Operations**: Do not bundle raw SQLite persistent binaries directly into serverless cloud runtimes like Vercel. Keep your serverless frontend assets cleanly decoupled from your physical database core node hardware.
